1 REM THE BYTE SIEVE (1981), FULL SIZE, USING THE K4510'S BANK REGISTERS:
2 REM (A DIM FLAGS(8191) ARRAY DIES OUT OF MEMORY: AN EHBASIC ELEMENT IS A
3 REM 6-BYTE FLOAT (8192 FLAGS = 48 KB). HERE BANK 1 MAPS 8 KB OF FAR
4 REM MEMORY AT $200000 INTO $2000-$3FFF AND EACH FLAG IS ONE POKED BYTE.
5 PRINT "BYTE SIEVE, 8191 FLAGS AS BYTES IN A BANKED WINDOW (SEE THE REMS)"
10 POKE 54788,0: POKE 54789,0: POKE 54790,32: POKE 54791,0: REM BANK 1 -> $200000
20 SZ=8190: B=8192: REM THE WINDOW AT $2000
30 T=PEEK(54541)+256*PEEK(54542)
40 CO=0
50 FOR I=0 TO SZ: POKE B+I,1: NEXT
60 FOR I=0 TO SZ
70 IF PEEK(B+I)=0 THEN 130
80 PR=I+I+3: K=I+PR
90 IF K>SZ THEN 120
100 POKE B+K,0: K=K+PR
110 GOTO 90
120 CO=CO+1
130 NEXT
140 PRINT CO;" PRIMES"
150 T=PEEK(54541)+256*PEEK(54542)-T: IF T<0 THEN T=T+65536
160 PRINT "TIME:";T;"FRAMES =";INT(T/0.6)/100;"SECONDS  (ONE ITERATION)"
170 PRINT "FOR SCALE: A STOCK C64 NEEDS SEVERAL MINUTES FOR ONE ITERATION."
180 PRINT "THE C VERSION (RUN SIEVE IN THE SHELL) DOES TEN IN 0.93 S."
190 POKE 54791,255: REM BANK 1 OFF
900 PRINT: PRINT "ANY KEY...";
905 GET K$: IF K$="" THEN 905
910 IF PEEK(1039) THEN LOAD "BENCH.BAS"
